The copyright line above is the single source of truth for this
project's attribution. It is checked against the per-file SPDX headers
by `npm run check:license`, so this file and the ~900 source headers
cannot drift apart silently.

Copyright holder and citation credit are deliberately separate fields.
CITATION.cff records who to cite for the software as scholarship; this
file and the file headers record who holds copyright in the code. See
CITATION.cff for the former.

Third-party dependency licences are not reproduced here. They are
resolved from the manifests that declare them — `package-lock.json` for
the npm tree and `src-tauri/Cargo.lock` for the Rust tree — which stay
accurate as those trees change in a way a hand-maintained list would
not.
